# CODEOWNERS for engineering-standards-central
#
# Governs PR review routing. The two rules below implement the access model
# described in docs/decision-records/0004-single-repo-distribution.md.
#
# - Default ownership covers source/, compiler/, schemas/, docs/, fixtures/,
#   tests/, tooling, and CI. PRs to these paths require review from at least
#   one member of @platform-team OR @standards-council per the
#   docs/02-implementation-plan.md §2.3 review SLA.
#
# - /dist/ is the compiled output tree. PRs touching it auto-request review
#   from the @engineering-standards-bot GitHub App identity. The App NEVER approves human
#   PRs — `dist/` is regenerated only by the release workflow (see Phase 7,
#   docs/02-implementation-plan.md §10). Human-authored modifications to
#   /dist/ are additionally rejected by the `dist-protection-lint` PR status
#   check (Phase 7) and by the opt-in client-side pre-commit hook at
#   tools/git-hooks/pre-commit (Phase 1).
#
# NOTE: The @platform-team, @standards-council, and @engineering-standards-bot handles
# must exist as GitHub Teams / GitHub App identities in the org before this
# file becomes load-bearing. Until then, CODEOWNERS still parses cleanly and
# documents intent; GitHub will silently drop reviewers for handles that do
# not yet exist (no PR is blocked).

# Default ownership — everything except /dist/.
*           @platform-team @standards-council

# Compiled distribution — read-only to humans; routed to the bot identity.
/dist/      @engineering-standards-bot
